      "sourceText": "AMS 102 - Elements of Statistics OR AMS 210 - Applied Linear Algebra; MAT 131 - Calculus I; MAT 132 - Calculus II; If students do not place into MAT 125 or MAT 131 on the basis of the math placement examination, MAT 123 (or MAT 119 /MAT 123) is a required course for the major.; MAT 203 - Calculus III with Applications OR AMS 261 - Applied Calculus III; CHE 131 - General Chemistry IB (Note: CHE 129 /CHE 130 or CHE 152 may be substituted for CHE 131 ); PHY 125, PHY 126, PHY 133, PHY 127, PHY 134 OR PHY 131, PHY 133, PHY 132, PHY 134 OR PHY 141, PHY 133, PHY 142, PHY 134; ESG 111 - Programming for Engineers OR PHY 277 - Computation for Physics and Astronomy OR CSE 130 - Introduction to Programming in C"
